{"tool_name":"ggip","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"ggip","home":"https://protein.b.dendai.ac.jp/GGIP/","summary":"A Web Server for GPCR-GPCR Interaction Pair Prediction.","addition_date":"2022-07-29T20:59:17.765486Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T14:15:18.896102Z","tool_type":["Web application"],"collections":["gpcr"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:ggip","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"w.nemoto@mail.dendai.ac.jp","name":"Wataru Nemoto","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Hiroyuki Toh"},{"name":"Vachiranee Limviphuvadh"},{"name":"Yoshihiro Yamanishi"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["mbermudez1"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1929"}]},{"data":{"term":"Structure","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0883"},"format":[{"term":"PDB","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1476"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Protein interaction prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2492"},{"term":"Protein structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0474"},{"term":"Sequence classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2995"},{"term":"Transmembrane protein prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0269"}]}],"name":"GGIP","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.3389/fendo.2022.825195","metadata":{"abstract":"The GGIP web server (https://protein.b.dendai.ac.jp/GGIP/) provides a web application for GPCR-GPCR interaction pair prediction by a support vector machine. The server accepts two sequences in the FASTA format. It responds with a prediction that the input GPCR sequence pair either interacts or not. GPCRs predicted to interact with the monomers constituting the pair are also shown when query sequences are human GPCRs. The server is simple to use. A pair of amino acid sequences in the FASTA format is pasted into the text area, a PDB ID for a template structure is selected, and then the \u2018Execute\u2019 button is clicked. The server quickly responds with a prediction result. The major advantage of this server is that it employs the GGIP software, which is presently the only method for predicting GPCR-interaction pairs. Our web server is freely available with no login requirement. In this article, we introduce some application examples of GGIP for disease-associated mutation analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Fujishiro S."},{"name":"Fukushima A."},{"name":"Limviphuvadh V."},{"name":"Nemoto W."},{"name":"Shimamura S."},{"name":"Toh H."},{"name":"Yamanishi Y."}],"citationCount":3,"date":"2022-03-24T00:00:00Z","journal":"Frontiers in Endocrinology","title":"A Web Server for GPCR-GPCR Interaction Pair Prediction"},"pmcid":"PMC8989088","pmid":"35399947"}],"topic":[{"term":"Bioinformatics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0091"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Membrane and lipoproteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0820"},{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Small molecules","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0154"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"GGIP","home":"https://bio.tools/ggip","summary":"A Web Server for GPCR-GPCR Interaction Pair Prediction.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:ggip/web/protein.b.dendai.ac.jp","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":4,"citations":[{"count":1,"year":"2022"},{"count":1,"year":"2026"},{"count":2,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.3389/fendo.2022.825195","pmcid":"PMC8989088","pmid":"35399947","ref_count":38,"refs":[{"count":1,"year":"1999"},{"count":1,"year":"2000"},{"co